{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>Then your light shall break forth like dawn.</b> That the light increases every moment." "<b>And your healing.</b> Your healing, and it is a noun, like אעלה ארוכה לך (I will raise up healing for you), and some say that ארוכתך means the days of the limit of the illness; therefore the word מהרה." "<b>And your righteousness shall go before you.</b> It shall gather you, like מאסף לכל המחנות (gatherer of all the camps) <small>(Numbers 10:25)</small>, and behold, it shall be kept."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 58, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:00:08.281436126Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}